The Helm charts under charts/gcp/ are ports of Cloud Foundation Fabric's
Terraform modules to Config Connector objects: their values, defaults,
validations, naming and outputs follow the modules they port, and their
descriptions quote the modules' variable descriptions. Each chart names
the module and the commit it was ported from in its Chart.yaml (sources
and the hfl.dev/source* annotations), in its README, and at the top of
each template, which also names the fabric file it ports and carries the
fabric file's copyright line. The pinned commits are in UPSTREAM.md.

The charts render Kubernetes objects for Config Connector
(https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/k8s-config-connector), Copyright
Google LLC, Apache-2.0. Its CRDs are fetched at test time by hack/kcc.sh
and are not in this repository.

This product also includes work derived from terraform-google-modules'
kubernetes-engine modules
(https://github.com/terraform-google-modules/terraform-google-kubernetes-engine),
Copyright Google LLC, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The
chart charts/gcp/gke-cluster ports modules/beta-private-cluster and
modules/beta-autopilot-private-cluster: its values, defaults, validations,
naming and outputs follow theirs, and its values.yaml quotes their variable
descriptions. Its Chart.yaml, README, upstream.yaml and the top of each
template name the commit and the files it ports, with their copyright line.

Other Terraform modules the catalog tracks
------------------------------------------

upstream/modules.yaml lists, besides fabric, the most-downloaded modules of
two more open-source sources, so that docs/coverage and the upstream
watcher can compare the catalog with them. No chart is derived from them
yet, and nothing of theirs is copied into this repository: the coverage
files record only the names and types of their variables and outputs, and
links to the modules.

- terraform-aws-modules (https://github.com/terraform-aws-modules), licensed
  under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The modules' LICENSE files carry no
  copyright line, except eventbridge ("Copyright 2021 Sven Lito"); none has a
  NOTICE file.
- Azure Verified Modules (https://github.com/Azure, the terraform-azurerm-avm-*
  and terraform-azure-avm-* repositories), licensed under the MIT License,
  Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation.

A chart ported from one of them will name the module and the commit it was
ported from, in the same places as the fabric charts, and carry that source's
licence text and copyright line in this file and at the top of its templates.
The Terraform in examples/ is modelled on the usage examples in the READMEs of
Cloud Foundation Fabric's modules (Apache-2.0, Copyright Google LLC), and the
files that follow one say so at the top. The rest of examples/ and docs/ is written
for this repository.
